# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# The one below is tracked on purpose.
#
# Android will only install an APK over an installed one when the two carry
# the same signature, so every build of OneBit has to share an identity.
# A GitHub runner starts with no `~/.android/debug.keystore`, which means
# AGP mints a fresh random key on each job and a release could never be
# installed over the previous release - sideloaded or from inside the app.
#
# This is the stock Android debug credential (alias `androiddebugkey`,
# password `android`), the same one `keytool` generates for every
# developer machine, so publishing it costs nothing an attacker with the
# default password did not already have.
!app/debug.keystore
